# Example ReRDMFT input file: continuing a CASSCF from RESTART files at another geometry (READ_RESTART), as in lih_gnof_read_restart.inp.
# 1) Run examples/casscf_lih.inp: it writes RESTART.NON_REL, RESTART.X2C and RESTART.4C (orbitals and CI vector).
# 2) Run this file from the same directory: the geometry is stretched to 1.70; the SCF is skipped, the orbitals are
#    Loewdin-orthonormalized at the new geometry, and the CI vector of the file starts the CI. The files are overwritten.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
CASSCF TRUE
CASSCF_ELECTRONS 2
CASSCF_SPINORS 4
READ_RESTART TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.700000
END
